From 2e5a8637caba942ffdb1e0c3d537e470b37390d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:40:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] S2-10 GBA: a live screen over the save, the load and
 the town build (dim / fade + card + spinner at 30 pictures a second)

plat_busy arms the SP5 load-fade watch with a 50 ms fuse (a save dims to half, a load or a build fades to black);
the first plat_busy_step after the fuse paints a small "Saving..." / "Loading..." card into the Mode 4 page on
screen from the main thread (vid_rect / vid_text), and from then on the VBlank hook turns its spinner every two
vblanks with a few raw halfword stores (no call, no DMA, no overlay code: it runs inside whatever the main thread
is doing: a flash sector, a scene's enter) and counts each step as a presented frame. The flip that ends the wait
lifts the fade as before and, when a card was painted, tells the page trackers (pn / hold / stage) that neither
page keeps a picture. Nothing happens in a run that hashes every frame (draw_all). EWRAM +16 B, IWRAM +0.

Steps added where the main thread otherwise holds the tick for tens of ms: the relationship graph's encode and
decode (every 32 edges), rel_normalize's sort, sim_init's per-citizen loop (cross-stream: one line in sim.c),
and every flash sector in save_flash.c.

New group gba/harness/scripts/speed2_busy.txt (title -> New story, new island, a Classic save and load, the
worst-case 58 KB island's save and load). GBA, mGBA, same commands before / after:
  save (Classic):    10,731 ms one frame -> 30.0 fps, worst picture gap 50 ms
  load (Classic):     6,513 ms -> 29.9 fps, worst gap 67 ms
  save (worst case): 11,245 ms -> 30.0 fps, worst gap 50 ms
  load (worst case):  7,803 ms -> 29.9 fps, worst gap 67 ms
  title -> New story: 2,076 ms -> 29.6 fps, worst gap 50 ms
  new island:         1,992 ms -> worst gap 117 ms (the hub's own 39 frames of 67-117 ms after it: S3-14)
Saved bytes identical: the 128 KB flash image of coresave1.txt (58 KB island in slot 1, a story island in slot 0)
is sha256-identical between the old and new ROM. Frame hashes (entry_parity + speed_tour, 98 windows): identical
with busy arming disabled; with it, only the frames after a new island's build differ (card, dim, trackers reset).

